Denmark,DNK,4.9  Can coercion be indirect?,Yes,Denmark considers that coercion is not limited to means of direct or indirect use of force and that also measures below this threshold may constitute coercion. Cyber activities that do not amount to use of force can therefore also be coercive.,"Denmark’s Position Paper on the Application of International Law in Cyberspace,",https://perma.cc/6D5U-ZXJ8,
