Denmark,DNK,7.2 Does the prohibition proscribe intervention in a state’s external (foreign) affairs?,Yes,"The scope of activities falling within the domaine réservé include but are not limited to “ (…) the choice of a political, economic, social, and cultural system, and the formulation of foreign policy.” The range of activities covered by the non-intervention rule largely overlap with the activities reserved to States under the rule of sovereignty.","Denmark’s Position Paper on the Application of International Law in Cyberspace,",https://perma.cc/6D5U-ZXJ8,
Denmark,DNK,7.3 Is the zone of protected sovereign prerogatives referred to as domaine réservé?,Yes,"In order for an action to qualify as an unlawful intervention it must qualify as an intervention in matters that are the sovereign prerogative of a State, the so-called domaine réservé, and it must involve an element of coercion.","Denmark’s Position Paper on the Application of International Law in Cyberspace,",https://perma.cc/6D5U-ZXJ8,
Denmark,DNK,"7.4 Is the domaine réservé limited to matters involving the state’s choice of a political, economic, social, and cultural system, and the formulation of foreign policy?",No,"The scope of activities falling within the domaine réservé include but are not limited to “ (…) the choice of a political, economic, social, and cultural system, and the formulation of foreign policy.” The range of activities covered by the non-intervention rule largely overlap with the activities reserved to States under the rule of sovereignty.","Denmark’s Position Paper on the Application of International Law in Cyberspace,",https://perma.cc/6D5U-ZXJ8,
Denmark,DNK,7.5 Does international law regulation over a matter of sovereign prerogative remove it from the domaine réservé?,Silent,,,,
Denmark,DNK,7.6 Is critical infrastructure part of the domaine réservé?,Silent,,,,
Denmark,DNK,7.7 Are elections part of the domaine réservé?,Yes,"The scope of activities falling within the domaine réservé include but are not limited to “ (…) the choice of a political, economic, social, and cultural system, and the formulation of foreign policy. An example of unlawful intervention in the cyber domain could be where a State coercively interferes in the internal political process of another. In the cyber context this could potentially occur by using cyber technology to alter electronic ballots and thereby affecting the results of a political election.","Denmark’s Position Paper on the Application of International Law in Cyberspace,",https://perma.cc/6D5U-ZXJ8,
