Estonia,EST,1. Is the prohibition of non-intervention a norm of customary international law?,Yes,"The principle of non-intervention is a well-established rule of international law, which flows from the principle of sovereignty, and applies to state conduct in Cyberspace.",UNGA Official Compendium of Voluntary National Contributions,https://perma.cc/UD7M-5NA7,
Estonia,EST,2. Is the scope of the principle of non-intervention uncertain?,Silent,"The principle of non-intervention is a well-established rule of international law, which flows from the principle of sovereignty, and applies to state conduct in cyberspace",UNGA Official Compendium of Voluntary National Contributions,https://perma.cc/UD7M-5NA7,
Estonia,EST,3. Does the prohibition of non-intervention apply to cyber-operations?,Yes,"¶2. The possibility for a cyber operation to constitute an unlawful intervention in the functions that form a part of a state’s domaine réservé has found acceptance among states, including Estonia, especially regarding the rights and obligations deriving from the principle of state sovereignty.",UNGA Official Compendium of Voluntary National Contributions,https://perma.cc/UD7M-5NA7,
Estonia,EST,4. Is coercion a constituent element of prohibited intervention?,Yes,"¶2. When discussing if a cyber operation constitutes an unlawful intervention into the external or internal affairs of another state, the element of coercion is a key factor.",UNGA Official Compendium of Voluntary National Contributions,https://perma.cc/UD7M-5NA7,
Estonia,EST,4.1 Is coercion limited to the employment of physical force?,Silent,,,,
Estonia,EST,4.2 Can dictatorial demands or acts of compulsion or imposition constitute coercion?,Silent,,,,
Estonia,EST,4.3 Does the deprivation of a State’s ability to control matters within its domaine réservé amount to coercion?,Silent,,,,
Estonia,EST,4.4 Does coercion extend to any affirmative acts designed to deprive another state of its freedom of choice with regard to a matter of protected sovereign prerogative?,Ambiguous,"¶2. Stemming from that, cyber operations that aim to force another nation to act in an involuntary manner or to refrain from acting in a certain manner, and target the other nation’s domaine réservé (e.g. national democratic processes such as elections, or military, security or critical infrastructure systems) could constitute such an intervention.",UNGA Official Compendium of Voluntary National Contributions,https://perma.cc/UD7M-5NA7,
Estonia,EST,4.5 Must there be a causal nexus between the responsible state’s actions/efforts and the effects on the target state’s internal or external affairs?,Silent,,,,
Estonia,EST,4.6 Can attempts to coerce an outcome amount to prohibited intervention?,Yes,"¶2. Stemming from that, cyber operations that aim to force another nation to act in an involuntary manner or to refrain from acting in a certain manner, and target the other nation’s domaine réservé (e.g. national democratic processes such as elections, or military, security or critical infrastructure systems) could constitute such an intervention.",UNGA Official Compendium of Voluntary National Contributions,https://perma.cc/UD7M-5NA7,
Estonia,EST,4.7 Is intent a constituent element of coercion?,Silent,,,,
Estonia,EST,"4.8 Must the action(s) constituting coercion be designed/intended to influence outcomes in, or conduct with respect to, a matter of protected sovereign prerogative?",Yes,"¶1. If an operation attributable to another state affects a state’s internal or external affairs in such a manner that it coerces a state to take a course of action it would not voluntarily seek, it would constitute a prohibited intervention.  ¶2. When discussing if a cyber operation constitutes an unlawful intervention into the external or internal affairs of another state, the element of coercion is a key factor... Stemming from that, cyber operations that aim to force another nation to act in an involuntary manner or to refrain from acting in a certain manner, and target the other nation’s domaine réservé (e.g. national democratic processes such as elections, or military, security or critical infrastructure systems) could constitute such an intervention.",UNGA Official Compendium of Voluntary National Contributions,https://perma.cc/UD7M-5NA7,
Estonia,EST,4.9  Can coercion be indirect?,Silent,,,,
Estonia,EST,4.10 Must the target state have knowledge of the coercive cyber operation constituting the purported intervention?,Silent,,,,
Estonia,EST,5. Does intervention include forms of persuasion or propaganda?,Silent,,,,
Estonia,EST,6. Is there a de minimis exception to the prohibition?,Silent,,,,
Estonia,EST,"7. Must the intervention be directed at matters over which the victim state is permitted by the principle of sovereignty, to decide freely?",Ambiguous,"¶2. The possibility for a cyber operation to constitute an unlawful intervention in the functions that form a part of a state’s domaine réservé has found acceptance among states, including Estonia, especially regarding the rights and obligations deriving from the principle of state sovereignty. States’ domaine réservé according to the ICJ includes the “choice of a political, economic, social, and cultural system, and the formulation of foreign policy.”",UNGA Official Compendium of Voluntary National Contributions,https://perma.cc/UD7M-5NA7,
Estonia,EST,7.1 Does the zone of protected sovereign prerogatives include only internal affairs?,No,"¶1. If an operation attributable to another state affects a state’s internal or external affairs in such a manner that it coerces a state to take a course of action it would not voluntarily seek, it would constitute a prohibited intervention.   ¶2. Stemming from that, cyber operations that aim to force another nation to act in an involuntary manner or to refrain from acting in a certain manner, and target the other nation’s domaine réservé (e.g. national democratic processes such as elections, or military, security or critical infrastructure systems) could constitute such an intervention.",UNGA Official Compendium of Voluntary National Contributions,https://perma.cc/UD7M-5NA7,
Estonia,EST,7.2 Does the prohibition proscribe intervention in a state’s external (foreign) affairs?,Yes,"¶2. The possibility for a cyber operation to constitute an unlawful intervention in the functions that form a part of a state’s domaine réservé has found acceptance among states, including Estonia, especially regarding the rights and obligations deriving from the principle of state sovereignty. States’ domaine réservé according to the ICJ includes the “choice of a political, economic, social, and cultural system, and the formulation of foreign policy.",UNGA Official Compendium of Voluntary National Contributions,https://perma.cc/UD7M-5NA7,
Estonia,EST,7.3 Is the zone of protected sovereign prerogatives referred to as domaine réservé?,Yes,"¶2. The possibility for a cyber operation to constitute an unlawful intervention in the functions that form a part of a state’s domaine réservé has found acceptance among states, including Estonia, especially regarding the rights and obligations deriving from the principle of state sovereignty. States’ domaine réservé according to the ICJ includes the “choice of a political, economic, social, and cultural system, and the formulation of foreign policy.",UNGA Official Compendium of Voluntary National Contributions,https://perma.cc/UD7M-5NA7,
Estonia,EST,"7.4 Is the domaine réservé limited to matters involving the state’s choice of a political, economic, social, and cultural system, and the formulation of foreign policy?",Ambiguous,"¶2. The possibility for a cyber operation to constitute an unlawful intervention in the functions that form a part of a state’s domaine réservé has found acceptance among states, including Estonia, especially regarding the rights and obligations deriving from the principle of state sovereignty. States’ domaine réservé according to the ICJ includes the “choice of a political, economic, social, and cultural system, and the formulation of foreign policy.",UNGA Official Compendium of Voluntary National Contributions,https://perma.cc/UD7M-5NA7,
