Republic of Korea,KOR,1. Is the prohibition of non-intervention a norm of customary international law?,Yes,"“As a logical consequence of the principle of sovereign equality, no State may intervene in the domestic affairs of another. This principle is explicitly codified in Article 2(7) of the UN Charter and has been affirmed in international jurisprudence. This principle applies equally in cyberspace”",National Position of the Republic of Korea on the Application of International Law in Cyberspace,https://perma.cc/P3W7-9URM,
Republic of Korea,KOR,2. Is the scope of the principle of non-intervention uncertain?,Silent,,,,
Republic of Korea,KOR,3. Does the prohibition of non-intervention apply to cyber-operations?,Yes,"“As a logical consequence of the principle of sovereign equality, no State may intervene in the domestic affairs of another. This principle is explicitly codified in Article 2(7) of the UN Charter and has been affirmed in international jurisprudence. This principle applies equally in cyberspace”",National Position of the Republic of Korea on the Application of International Law in Cyberspace,https://perma.cc/P3W7-9URM,
