Singapore,SGP,"7. Must the intervention be directed at matters over which the victim state is permitted by the principle of sovereignty, to decide freely?",Yes,"5. A prohibited intervention by one State against another must have a bearing on matters in which the victim State is permitted, by the principle of State sovereignty, to decide freely, including its choice of a political, economic, social and cultural system, and the formulation of foreign policy.","Singapore, UNGA Official Compendium of Voluntary National Contributions, pg. 83, ¶ 5 (2021).",https://perma.cc/UD7M-5NA7,
Singapore,SGP,7.1 Does the zone of protected sovereign prerogatives include only internal affairs?,No,"5. Singapore affirms that the principle of non-intervention in the internal affairs of other States applies to cyberspace...A prohibited intervention by one State against another must have a bearing on matters in which the victim State is permitted, by the principle of State sovereignty, to decide freely, including its choice of a political, economic, social and cultural system, and the formulation of foreign policy.","Singapore, UNGA Official Compendium of Voluntary National Contributions, pg. 83, ¶ 5 (2021)",https://perma.cc/UD7M-5NA7,
Singapore,SGP,7.2 Does the prohibition proscribe intervention in a state’s external (foreign) affairs?,Yes,"5. A prohibited intervention by one State against another must have a bearing on matters in which the victim State is permitted, by the principle of State sovereignty, to decide freely, including its choice of a political, economic, social and cultural system, and the formulation of foreign policy.","Singapore, UNGA Official Compendium of Voluntary National Contributions, pg. 83, ¶ 5 (2021).",https://perma.cc/UD7M-5NA7,
