Sweden,SWE,1. Is the prohibition of non-intervention a norm of customary international law?,Yes,“The principle of non-intervention is a fundamental principle of international law also applicable in cyberspace.”,"Sweden’s Position Paper on the Application of International Law in Cyberspace , pg. 2, (2022).",https://tuprd-my.sharepoint.com/:b:/r/personal/tup46628_temple_edu/Documents/iLIT%20Projects/iLIT%20RA%20Files/Working%20Folders%20%5BActive%20Projects%5D/Cyber/National%20Cyber%20Statements/Source%20Materials/National%20Statements/Sweden/swedens-position-paper-on-the-application-of-international-law-in-cyberspace.pdf?csf=1&web=1&e=OhgEhI,
Sweden,SWE,2. Is the scope of the principle of non-intervention uncertain?,Ambiguous,"“The prohibition of intervention is generally understood to include two elements: intervening in matters in which each State is permitted to decide freely, and the involvement of coercion.”","Sweden’s Position Paper on the Application of International Law in Cyberspace , pg. 3, (2022).",https://tuprd-my.sharepoint.com/:b:/r/personal/tup46628_temple_edu/Documents/iLIT%20Projects/iLIT%20RA%20Files/Working%20Folders%20%5BActive%20Projects%5D/Cyber/National%20Cyber%20Statements/Source%20Materials/National%20Statements/Sweden/swedens-position-paper-on-the-application-of-international-law-in-cyberspace.pdf?csf=1&web=1&e=OhgEhI,
Sweden,SWE,3. Does the prohibition of non-intervention apply to cyber-operations?,Yes,“The principle of non-intervention is a fundamental principle of international law also applicable in cyberspace.”,"Sweden’s Position Paper on the Application of International Law in Cyberspace , pg. 2, (2022).",https://tuprd-my.sharepoint.com/:b:/r/personal/tup46628_temple_edu/Documents/iLIT%20Projects/iLIT%20RA%20Files/Working%20Folders%20%5BActive%20Projects%5D/Cyber/National%20Cyber%20Statements/Source%20Materials/National%20Statements/Sweden/swedens-position-paper-on-the-application-of-international-law-in-cyberspace.pdf?csf=1&web=1&e=OhgEhI,
Sweden,SWE,4. Is coercion a constituent element of prohibited intervention?,Yes,"“The prohibition of intervention is generally understood to include two elements: intervening in matters in which each State is permitted to decide freely, and the involvement of coercion. These elements were confirmed by the International Court of Justice (ICJ) in the Nicaragua case.”","Sweden’s Position Paper on the Application of International Law in Cyberspace , pg. 3, (2022).",https://tuprd-my.sharepoint.com/:b:/r/personal/tup46628_temple_edu/Documents/iLIT%20Projects/iLIT%20RA%20Files/Working%20Folders%20%5BActive%20Projects%5D/Cyber/National%20Cyber%20Statements/Source%20Materials/National%20Statements/Sweden/swedens-position-paper-on-the-application-of-international-law-in-cyberspace.pdf?csf=1&web=1&e=OhgEhI,
