Sweden,SWE,7.1 Does the zone of protected sovereign prerogatives include only internal affairs?,Ambiguous,"“In the Friendly Relations Declaration, the principle of non-intervention is explained as ‘No State or group of States has the right to intervene, directly or indirectly, for any reason whatever, in the internal or external affairs of any other State.’”","Sweden’s Position Paper on the Application of International Law in Cyberspace , pg. 2-3, (2022).",https://tuprd-my.sharepoint.com/:b:/r/personal/tup46628_temple_edu/Documents/iLIT%20Projects/iLIT%20RA%20Files/Working%20Folders%20%5BActive%20Projects%5D/Cyber/National%20Cyber%20Statements/Source%20Materials/National%20Statements/Sweden/swedens-position-paper-on-the-application-of-international-law-in-cyberspace.pdf?csf=1&web=1&e=OhgEhI,
